TRANSLATE (the 3rd operator): does replicating a working detector beat learning each position?
N=16 K=3, 14 positions, 40 seeds x 3 restarts. translation-invariant motif task.
SHARED = one filter tiled at every position (a convolution), 3 filter weights.
INDEP  = a separate filter per position (locally connected), 42 filter weights.

fair stats: mean over restarts (no best-of), mean +/- std over seeds.
  train size | SHARED (weight-shared) | INDEP (per-position)  | gap
  16         | 0.820 +/- 0.122       | 0.581 +/- 0.065      | +0.239
  32         | 0.838 +/- 0.094       | 0.615 +/- 0.071      | +0.224
  64         | 0.866 +/- 0.082       | 0.672 +/- 0.076      | +0.195
  128        | 0.867 +/- 0.081       | 0.724 +/- 0.086      | +0.143

translation pays if SHARED matches/beats INDEP at 14x fewer weights, and the gap grows as data
shrinks -- one working module tiled across positions learns from all of them (data efficiency).
